Description: Stream Deck manager for GNOME
 Veranda is a modern GTK4 / libadwaita application for managing Elgato Stream
 Deck devices on Linux, built to feel native to GNOME. Drag actions onto keys
 to launch apps, run commands, press hotkeys, type text, or build macros, and
 arrange them across pages and profiles. Live "Special Buttons" turn keys into
 glanceable widgets such as a clock, now playing, battery, or volume.
 .
 The python-elgato-streamdeck library ("streamdeck" on PyPI) is vendored into
 this package at build time, as it is not yet in the Debian archive.
